{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A1","title_html":"A1","html":"<p>A rate model uses person-years as the exposure. A colleague\nre-expresses exposure in person-months, multiplying every <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"t_i\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D456 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> by twelve. Which coefficients change\nand by how much? Which fitted values change?</p>","file":"ch37-counts/02-offsets-and-rates.html"}